\begin{abstract}
We present the Universal Code Simulation Engine (UCSE), a unified,
multi-scale physical law framework capable of evolving quantum,
relativistic, plasma, and cosmological domains under a single invariant
action. UCSE integrates gauge theory, holographic entropy, general
relativity, quantum information, and relativistic hydrodynamics into a
continuous computational manifold spanning $10^{-35}$ to $10^{26}$ m.
Empirical validation is performed using Planck 2018 TT/TE/EE+lensing
spectra, Gaia DR3 astrometry, LIGO/Virgo O3/O4 gravitational wave strain
data, and NIST Dirac-Fock relativistic atomic baselines. UCSE achieves
sub-$0.05\sigma$ agreement with cosmological parameters, near-perfect
gravitational waveform matching ($F = 0.99984$), anomaly-free gauge
behavior ($\mathcal{A}_{\text{gauge}} < 10^{-18}$), and symplectic
energy conservation ($\Delta H/H_0 < 10^{-13}$). These results establish
UCSE as a unified, empirically validated physical law engine.
